# Everything scripts/sign-zones.sh produces is a regenerated artifact,
# not a source file -- the assignment's own Git-hygiene rule is
# explicit about this: "commit sources, configs, and scripts only --
# not artifacts your scripts regenerate (compiled binaries, SIGNED
# ZONES, built Docker images, and the like)." The grader re-runs your
# script from the plain .zone sources to rebuild all of this.
**/*.private
**/*.key
**/*.signed
**/*.ds
**/dsset-*
**/*.zone.signing
resolver/trust-anchor.conf
client/trust-anchor.conf
